cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite Version 0.1.0 of this research repository."
title: "Total variation under largest-prime deletion"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Kline
    given-names: Jeffery
repository-code: "https://github.com/jeff-kline/largest-prime-deletion"
url: "https://github.com/jeff-kline/largest-prime-deletion"
license: GPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  A paper and release repository on deleting the K largest prime factors of a
  uniformly random squarefree integer at most n. It proves that the total
  variation distance between the laws of the remaining integer at depths K and
  K+1 has limit superior in n of order (log K)^(-1/4). The proof extends the
  multiplier-comparison method of Richter and Bergelson-Richter with a weighted
  Fourier matching estimate, uniform in the window width, for products of
  primes from moving windows. Testing against the Moebius function gives
  M(n)=o(n). The argument does not assume the prime number theorem; it uses
  elementary prime estimates and Plancherel's theorem. It gives no rate for
  M(n)/n and no new prime number theorem error term, and the statement of the
  deletion theorem alone is not claimed as new; the rate is not claimed to be
  sharp.
keywords:
  - largest prime factor
  - total variation
  - squarefree integers
  - Moebius function
  - Mertens function
  - prime number theorem
references:
